{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And acacia wood.</b> In the wilderness there were forests in which grew those trees called שטים, and thus it is written: 'וישב ישראל בשטים.' The wood was light and smooth and fine. And it appears that it was very light, for all the forty-eight planks — their sockets, their bars, and all the posts of the court and their sockets, and the nine posts of the Tabernacle and their sockets, and their pegs — all together were carried on eight wagons given to the sons of Merari, as detailed in the portion of במדבר ונשא, even though the planks were large beams of ten cubits in length, a cubit and a half in width, and a cubit in thickness. Rather, it is certainly a choice wood and very light."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:17.200190401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}